content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-114, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-20500, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: 8.3 mm/s at the drive-end bearing housing. The applicable manufacturer criterion is Figure 3, vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The reading is above the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/D boundary and within Zone D (7.1–11.0), labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. This is the manufacturer's highest severity zone, so SSP-07 requires immediate shutdown and notification of the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-housing temperature: 70 C. HF-300 temperatures are measured on the housing surface; normal is up to 70 C, alarm is 80 C and trip is 90 C. The reading is therefore at the upper normal limit, below both alarm and trip. It does not meet SSP-07's temperature criterion of above the manufacturer's alarm limit for raising a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: none reported. No numerical leakage limit is supplied. The troubleshooting table's leakage-driven mechanical-seal replacement is not triggered by this report, although absence of leakage does not establish the internal condition of the seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment: listed first among the manual's probable causes of high vibration; check alignment before dismantling and after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear: inspect the bearings. The drive-end measurement location alone does not prove that only the drive-end bearing is defective; if either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage: inspect the impeller as part of the high-vibration troubleshooting scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation: check NPSH. No suction-condition or NPSH results are supplied to confirm or exclude this cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-114 immediately and keep it stopped under the Zone D instruction. Notify the reliability engineer of the highest-severity-zone vibration and ensure the engineer is notified before any restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the line; then obtain the line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before dismantling, investigate the as-found high-vibration causes without restarting the stopped pump solely for data collection. Check shaft alignment using a laser tool: parallel-offset tolerance 0.05 mm and angular tolerance 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Review available process information for the required NPSH check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If internal access is required, use the back pull-out arrangement, which allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg: use certified lifting equipment and a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor because it exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and impeller and complete the NPSH/cavitation investigation. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace drive-end bearing HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 (6310-C3) together as a pair. Do not condemn or replace the impeller without an inspection finding.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, apply Table 5 only to fasteners actually disturbed, with lightly oiled threads: M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M16 casing bolts 210 Nm. If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not include mechanical-seal replacement in the base scope solely from this no-leakage report. If inspection separately authorises seal replacement, follow procedure 5.2, inspect the sleeve for scoring, fit HF3-450 and a new casing gasket, and tighten M10 seal-gland nuts to 25 Nm on lightly oiled threads. Do not apply HF3-450B or its 30 Nm torque to this below-bulletin serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any repair that moves the motor or bearing housing, repeat laser alignment and meet parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm that the reliability engineer has been notified. Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. At the first running check, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3 and act on that zone; stop again if it remains in Zone D. Record housing-surface temperature against normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C and trip 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; contingency quantity for the bearing-repair scope, to be replaced together with HF3-510 if either bearing meets the manual's replacement condition.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; contingency quantity for the required bearing-pair replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit a new gasket whenever the casing is opened and during mechanical-seal replacement. Not required merely for use of the back pull-out feature if the casing remains undisturbed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Component-type mechanical seal; contingency only if inspection separately authorises seal replacement. This is the applicable seal for serial HF3-20500, not HF3-450B.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediate equipment control: Zone D vibration requires the pump to be stopped now; SSP-07 also requires reliability-engineer notification before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal pump or seal work: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For removal of the 68 kg back pull-out assembly: a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required because the load exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-protection/operating control: seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge; never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical exposure control is conditional: if the raw-water line is chemically dosed, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The report does not establish whether dosing is present.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement, pair: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, applicable only if inspection establishes the manual's bearing-replacement condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment when performed: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician; alignment is required after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement only if separately authorised: standard time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. It is not included as a leakage-driven base task because no leakage was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual lists component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 gives M10 seal-gland nuts 25 Nm. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead requires cartridge seal HF3-450B and 30 Nm, but only for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-114 is serial HF3-20500, below that range; the bulletin explicitly says pumps below HF3-22000 continue using HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Therefore HF3-450 and 25 Nm apply if seal work is authorised; HF3-450B and 30 Nm do not apply to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bulletin's instruction to replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm is within its instructions for pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. It is not applied here as a documented rejection limit for HF3-20500. For this asset, procedure 5.2 requires sleeve inspection for scoring but supplies no numerical rejection depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 8.3 mm/s is an RMS vibration-velocity measurement on the bearing housing, as required by Figure 3. Only the drive-end reading is reported; the non-drive-end reading and weekly history are needed when they can be obtained without violating the Zone D stop, because the manual requires weekly measurement of both housings and classification of the highest reading (C06, C07).",
    "What are the suction conditions and NPSH results? The manual requires an NPSH check for high vibration but provides neither site data nor a numerical acceptance criterion in the supplied evidence (C09).",
    "Final repair scope depends on the alignment, bearing, impeller and cavitation findings. Table 6 provides no standard labour time for diagnosis, internal inspection, NPSH investigation or post-repair testing, so those durations require planning after the findings are known (C09, C10, C12).",
    "Is the raw-water transfer line chemically dosed? If it is, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory; the fault report does not establish dosing status (C15).",
    "If the shaft sleeve is exposed and scoring is found, obtain an engineering rejection criterion for serial HF3-20500. The manual requires inspection but gives no depth limit, while the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion is scoped to HF3-22000 and above (C10, C13).",
    "Confirm the site's work-order priority convention. SSP-07 explicitly assigns priority 1 for bearing temperature above the alarm limit, which is not met at 70 C, but gives no P1/P2/P3 mapping for Zone D vibration. P1 is selected conservatively here because immediate shutdown is mandatory, not because of the temperature reading (C02, C07, C15)."
  ]
}
